  "privacyPolicyTitle": "Privacy policy",
  "accessibilityTitle": "Accessibility statement",
  "privacyPolicyText": "Monako privacy policy (plain language)\n\n1. What we collect\n• Your email address, if you create an account.\n• Your notes (strokes, text, highlights) and the PDFs or images you import.\n• Your visual profiles (colours, sizes, filters) and your settings.\nWe never ask you to name a condition. We collect no advertising data and use no tracking tools.\n\n2. Why\nOnly to show your notes in your colours and sync them between your devices.\n\n3. Sensitive data\nA visual profile may reveal a health need. It is therefore:\n• stored in your private account, accessible only to you (even when you share a notebook, your profile is never shared);\n• encrypted in transit (HTTPS) and at rest (server and device);\n• never sold, never shared with advertisers.\nText recognition (OCR) happens on your device.\n\n4. Hosting\nData is hosted by Supabase (Postgres database, file storage and authentication).\n\n5. Your rights\n• Export all your data (Settings › Export my data).\n• Delete your account: your notes, profiles and files are erased immediately (within 30 days at most in backups).\n• Sign out: data is removed from the device.\n\n6. Minors\nIf you are under 14 (Quebec) or if your school requires it, a parent or guardian must consent to the account creation.\n\n7. Legal framework\nPersonal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) and, in Quebec, Law 25. For any question, contact the privacy officer listed on the app's store page.",
  "accessibilityText": "Accessibility statement\n\nMonako aims to conform to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, level AA, across its interface.\n\nWhat the app offers:\n• The whole interface is recoloured by your profile: never forced pure white or pure black.\n• Touch targets of at least 44 pt / 48 dp.\n• VoiceOver (iOS) and TalkBack (Android) support: every button has a name.\n• Respects the system text size.\n• No flashing; fades of 200 ms at most.\n• No information conveyed by colour alone: each ink has a number, a pattern or an icon.\n• Interface in French and English.\n• Rescue gesture: a triple tap restores a readable profile.\n\nKnown limitations:\n• A poor-quality scanned PDF without recognised text only gets the colour filter.\n• Charts with colour legends may lose meaning after recolouring: use “See the original”.\n\nReport a problem: write to us from the app's store page. We reply within 10 business days."
